1. (!x3 & x2 & !x1)
2. (!x3 & x2 & x1)
3. (x3 & !x2 & x1)
4. (x3 & x2 & x1)

The final Boolean expression for f is:
f = ((!x3 & x2 & !x1) | (!x3 & x2 & x1) | (x3 & !x2 & x1) | (x3 & x2 & x1)).

This expression can be implemented using AND gates for each product term, followed by a single OR gate to combine the outputs of the AND gates. The design ensures that the logic is clear and that the output f is computed directly from the inputs without any intermediate states or dependencies."
}
